{"blocks":[["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-3550","Recall to Computer copies the MicroFreak's current wavetables into a new bank in the computer pane. The bank initially has a date-and-time name, which you can change in the Bank Name field.",["14.2.2.1 Wavetable Management"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/01%20Management/Asset/01-Wavetable-management-buttons/png/","source-block-57","01 Wavetable management buttons",[]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/01%20Management/Asset/02-New-Bank-name-prompt/png/","source-block-57","02 New Bank name prompt",[]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/01%20Management/Asset/03-Import-choices/png/","source-block-57","03 Import choices",[]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/01%20Management/Asset/04-Export-choices/png/","source-block-57","04 Export choices",[]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/01%20Management/Asset/05-Delete-confirmation/png/","source-block-57","05 Delete confirmation",[]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/01%20Management/Asset/06-Wavetable-transfer-progress/png/","source-block-57","06 Wavetable transfer progress",[]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/02%20Dragging/","source-block-306","14.2.2.2 More on Dragging and Dropping",[]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/02%20Dragging/","source-block-349","Drag individual wavetables between the computer and MicroFreak in either direction. Shift-click or Command-click to select several before dragging.",["14.2.2.2 More on Dragging and Dropping"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/02%20Dragging/","source-block-500","A destination slot highlights blue when you hover over it. Releasing the wavetable there overwrites that slot.",["14.2.2.2 More on Dragging and Dropping"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/02%20Dragging/","source-block-614","Dragging a wavetable between computer and MicroFreak",["14.2.2.2 More on Dragging and Dropping"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/02%20Dragging/","source-block-965","Drag a wavetable within either pane to change its order. In the computer pane, drag a wavetable name over another bank's name to move it into that bank.",["14.2.2.2 More on Dragging and Dropping"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/02%20Dragging/","source-block-1121","WAV and AIFF files can also be dragged from a file browser into either pane. Select several files with Shift-click or Command-click before dragging them together.",["14.2.2.2 More on Dragging and Dropping"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/02%20Dragging/Asset/01-Dragging-a-wavetable-between-computer-and-MicroFreak/png/","source-block-57","01 Dragging a wavetable between computer and MicroFreak",[]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/02%20Wavetables%20Tab/Asset/01-Tab-for-loading-user-Wavetables/png/","source-block-57","01 Tab for loading user Wavetables",[]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/","source-block-242","14.2.3 Samples Tab",[]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/","source-block-265","The Samples tab appears when MIDI Control Center detects a connected MicroFreak with current firmware. It loads user samples for the Sample oscillator and the Scan Grains, Cloud Grains, and Hit Grains oscillator types.",["14.2.3 Samples Tab"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/","source-block-487","Tab for loading user samples",["14.2.3 Samples Tab"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/","source-block-747","The left pane shows banks and samples on the computer; the right pane shows samples in the MicroFreak.",["14.2.3 Samples Tab"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/","source-block-853","The information area shows the selected bank and sample names, sample length, total sample memory used, and remaining memory, with times displayed in seconds. Click a name field to rename the bank or sample.",["14.2.3 Samples Tab"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/","source-block-1064","Sample information area",["14.2.3 Samples Tab"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-225","14.2.3.1 Sample Management",[]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-256","The buttons above the panes manage samples on the computer and in the MicroFreak.",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-341","Sample management buttons",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-610","New Bank creates an empty bank on the computer and prompts for a name. Drag samples from other banks over the new bank's name to combine them.",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-760","New Bank name prompt",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-1014","Del Bank deletes a bank after confirmation. Factory banks cannot be deleted.",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-1098","Import offers three choices:",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-1134","Replace Sample (.mfsz) replaces the selected sample with a MicroFreak Sample file.",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management","Import offers three choices:"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-1225","Replace Sample (.wav/.aiff) replaces it with a WAV or AIFF audio file.",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management","Import offers three choices:"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-1304","Import New Bank adds an MFSBZ bank to the computer pane.",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management","Import offers three choices:"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-1369","Import choices",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-1729","Export saves the selected sample as MFSZ or the selected bank as MFSBZ. Choose a location in the system save dialog.",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-1853","Export choices",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-2089","Delete removes a selected sample after confirmation and replaces it with an init sample.",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management"]],["Microfreak/UG/14%20Config/02%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/03%20Samples%20Tab/01%20Management/","source-block-2185","Delete confirmation",["14.2.3.1 Sample Management"]]],"format_version":5}